#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'
Knowledge Hub Interactive Lab
TLS: Certificate Hostname Verification

Scenario
  Nginx serves HTTPS correctly, and the certificate is signed by the lab CA.
  Clients connect as app.internal, but the certificate SAN names the wrong host.

Goal
  Repair /workspace/tls.cnf so the issued server certificate is valid for:
    app.internal

Start here
  status
  openssl x509 -in tls/server.crt -noout -subject -ext subjectAltName
  openssl x509 -in tls/server.crt -noout -checkhost app.internal
  cat tls.cnf

Workflow
  nano tls.cnf
  apply
  check

Lab commands
  help    show this assignment again
  status  inspect the certificate and HTTPS endpoint
  check   verify chain, hostname and a real HTTPS request
  hint    reveal progressive help
  apply   regenerate the certificate and restart Nginx
  reset   restore the wrong hostname certificate

When finished, run: check
EOF
